-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- User guide
-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
UPDATE interface_templates
SET user_guide = $GUIDE$
# HL7 over TCP/IP

## Who this is for

Any lab instrument whose own setup screen lets you choose **HL7** as the
protocol and **TCP/IP / Network / Ethernet** as the connection type — not
serial/RS232, and not "ASTM". This covers many Mindray, Roche, Abbott, and
similar chemistry/hematology analyzers. If your instrument's manual instead
says "ASTM" or "RS232/Serial Port", this template is not the right fit —
see the note at the bottom.

## What you need before you start

- A network cable from the instrument to the same network this server is reachable on
- Access to the instrument's own LIS/host communication settings screen
- Your hospital's HIS results-delivery endpoint (ask your HIS vendor/admin if you don't already have it)

## Setup steps

1. **Pick a port number.** The default above is already chosen to work with this deployment -- you can keep it unless you have a reason to change it.
2. **On the instrument itself**, open its LIS/host communication setup screen, choose the **HL7** protocol (not ASTM), and enter this server's network address plus the **same port number** you entered above.
3. **"Does this instrument ask for the order before running a test?"** -- most analyzers that support this can work either way:
   - **Off (default)**: the instrument just sends results after running a test. Simplest setup.
   - **On**: the instrument will pause and ask this system for pending orders before running each sample -- only turn this on if the instrument's own settings screen is configured for "bidirectional" or "host query" mode.
4. **Enter your Results Delivery API URL.** This is where completed test results get sent.
5. If you turned the order-lookup toggle on, also enter your **Order-Lookup API URL** if you have one. If you don't have this yet, you can leave it blank for now -- the instrument will still get a valid reply, it just won't contain a real order (see note below).

## A note on bidirectional/host-query mode

When the toggle above is on, this system will answer the instrument's own live question ("what's ordered for this sample?") in real time, while the sample is sitting on the instrument waiting for an answer. Out of the box, this template's answer-building step is a **placeholder** -- it always replies "no pending order found" so the instrument gets a valid response instead of hanging, but it does not yet look up a real order from your HIS. An integration engineer needs to connect that step to your actual HIS's order-lookup API before this mode is fully useful in production -- ask ezHealthKonnect support or your integrator if you need help with that step.

## Advanced tuning

Acknowledgment timing/wording and detailed host-query settings (message types, timeout, failure behavior) can be fine-tuned later in **Pipeline Builder**, under this interface's connector step's **Acknowledgment** and **Host Query** tabs -- the defaults here cover the common case.

## If your instrument uses ASTM or a Serial (RS232) connection instead

Those are **not supported yet**. ASTM and raw serial-port connectivity are
a different protocol/transport combination that this platform doesn't have
a working connector for today -- using this template with that kind of
instrument will not work. This is a named, planned gap, not a hidden one;
ask your integrator about timing if you need it.
$GUIDE$
WHERE slug = 'device-hl7-tcp';
